FW: That my past will never be forgotten, not only forgotten, but I live it every day. And I only want the world to know that our [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] Holocaust-- you cannot call a Holocaust any other disaster because it was so unique, because Hitler wanted to exterminate every Jew-- child, woman. It's not like you have against somebody something that you take clergy, that you take people, influential people, that you take the intelligentsia. Here every Jew-- I want the world to know that every victim was not Jew-- not a Jew. But every Jew was a victim. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS]

And we are proud grandparents. [SIGHS] My daughter is in New York. My son lives here. And thank god that we've made it, that we didn't miss the boat. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS] What else? I don't know.

